### Private VNC backend independent review (IND450)

- Result: PASS for `manual/{backend,helper,private_channel,x11cleanup}.py` and `tests/test_ext_vnc_backend.py`; no blocking correctness, security, or simplification finding. Read repository instructions, Code Simplifier skill, MB-03–MB-11, PA-14, design §7 and manual API/private backend contracts. Domain service/DAO/DTO boundaries remain separate; backend owns only its private channel and helper tree. Structured pinned x11vnc `-inetd` invocation separates binary stdout from discarded native stderr, creates no backend listener or credential, and uses VNC_HELPER confinement without profile data or private state mounts/environment. Durable helper claim precedes X attachment; cancellation/EOF prevents late attach. Independent supervisor arms its initial watchdog before the first heartbeat, clamps sliding heartbeat deadlines to 60 seconds and the absolute cleanup bound, and makes loss/stop irreversible. Host plus PID/start identity protects owned cleanup, retained receipts require complete descendant exit before DEAD, and receipt-write failure leaves UNKNOWN. Input release uses only the verified private X context; browser/display/capacity are preserved.
